# Cloudflare Pages response headers. tools/build.mjs copies this file into dist/.
#
# A load never waits on the network for the theme: for a week after each load, the browser uses the copy it
# has at once and fetches any new file in the background, so a deploy reaches a returning user on the second
# full load after it. Past the week it waits for the check, as with no-cache. A no-cache directive here
# cancels the background fetch, and a longer max-age holds a deploy back until it runs out.
#
# Cloudflare-CDN-Cache-Control keeps the domain's own cache out of it. On a custom domain the zone also raises
# a max-age below its Browser Cache TTL to that TTL, so the hostname needs a Cache Rule with Browser TTL set to
# Respect origin.
/*
  Cache-Control: max-age=0, stale-while-revalidate=604800
  Cloudflare-CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
